## Why This Is Asked
Handles a realistic, repeatable issue in multi-tenant Linux environments. Evaluates practical debugging, safe isolation, and rollback discipline.

## Key Concepts
- inotify and max_user_watches
- per-tenant resource control (ulimit, cgroups)
- observability and test planning
- safe rollback

## Code Example
```javascript
// Simple Node.js watcher demo illustrating per-tenant file activity
const fs = require('fs');
const path = '/ci-scratch/tenant-A';
fs.watch(path, {recursive: true}, (ev, f) => {
  console.log(`[watch] ${ev}: ${f}`);
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you automate per-tenant limit adjustments and verification?
- How would you validate rollback in a production window without impacting running builds?

## Why This Is Asked

This situation tests ability to design robust multi-tenant resource governance with BPF maps, a common source of memory leaks in real-world deployments.

## Key Concepts

- BPF map accounting per tenant
- Map lifecycle and eviction strategies
- Namespace/isolation boundaries
- Observability with bpftool, perf, pidstat
- Canary rollouts and rollback plans

## Code Example

```c
// Pseudo: enforce per-tenant map limit
struct tenant {
  __u32 id;
  __u64 limit; // bytes
  __u64 used;
};
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you handle bursts exceeding quotas without impacting others?
- What metrics and alerts would you implement?

## Why This Is Asked
Examines ability to tame CPU scheduling and memory reclaim in multi-tenant Linux deployments under bursty workloads.

## Key Concepts
- cgroup v2 cpu.max and CPU weight for per-tenant QoS
- cpuset and CPU affinity to confine tenants
- memory reclaim behavior and swappiness tuning
- BPF-based observability for per-tenant latency, IRQs, cache misses
- phased testing, safe rollback, and controlled rollouts

## Code Example
```javascript
// Lightweight latency probe template (pseudo)
async function measureLatency(endpoint){
  const t0 = performance.now();
  await fetch(endpoint);
  return performance.now() - t0;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you quantify safe rollback criteria during staged tests?
- Which metrics dashboards and alerts would you configure for sustained SLOs?
